  "what_stands_in_their_place": [
   "seven 22A validators under --check, one of which executes all six replays",
   "a chronology row over every record that carries the pre-registration's hash",
   "the two released cross-domain gates, domain_smoke_test and domain.py health",
   "fourteen rows recorded from sealed W0 through W4 evidence, including the silo regression's zero and the boundary W2 handed to this matrix by name"
  ],
  "what_this_matrix_still_does_not_cover": "the hostile-package suite is not re-run here. Refusing a package is only evidence if the package could otherwise have reached a store, so the suite runs against 22A's database; `every_hostile_package_refused` and `nothing_registered_halfway` record W3's result and bind its bytes instead",
  "why": "every one of them reads a learning-surface store or a certification corpus. 22A registers domains and touches nothing that learns, so those rows would report on a surface this sprint did not change. Naming them is the point: a reader should not have to count rows to discover which claims are not made"
 },
